,7:headers;1617:40:4:Date,29:Mon, 06 Apr 2026 10:10:22 GMT,]52:12:Content-Type,32:text/event-stream; charset=utf-8,]31:17:Transfer-Encoding,7:chunked,]28:10:Connection,10:keep-alive,]28:13:Cache-Control,8:no-cache,]52:38:anthropic-ratelimit-input-tokens-limit,7:4000000,]56:42:anthropic-ratelimit-input-tokens-remaining,7:3999000,]66:38:anthropic-ratelimit-input-tokens-reset,20:2026-04-06T10:10:21Z,]52:39:anthropic-ratelimit-output-tokens-limit,6:800000,]56:43:anthropic-ratelimit-output-tokens-remaining,6:800000,]67:39:anthropic-ratelimit-output-tokens-reset,20:2026-04-06T10:10:21Z,]45:34:anthropic-ratelimit-requests-limit,4:4000,]49:38:anthropic-ratelimit-requests-remaining,4:3999,]62:34:anthropic-ratelimit-requests-reset,20:2026-04-06T10:10:21Z,]46:32:anthropic-ratelimit-tokens-limit,7:4800000,]50:36:anthropic-ratelimit-tokens-remaining,7:4799000,]60:32:anthropic-ratelimit-tokens-reset,20:2026-04-06T10:10:21Z,]46:10:request-id,28:req_011CZnLSh8NqighBtF4HBVZM,]77:25:strict-transport-security,44:max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload,]69:25:anthropic-organization-id,36:19d39eaa-efb4-49e0-afe8-a7359703719a,]23:6:Server,10:cloudflare,]39:29:x-envoy-upstream-service-time,3:904,]45:13:server-timing,24:x-originResponse;dur=906,]29:15:cf-cache-status,7:DYNAMIC,]207:10:set-cookie,188:_cfuvid=Zec8Jn447F.rrnW926R8HzIf4mHHn8ZlGmMaGkQHBi0-1775470221.834664-1.0.1.1-6qP1th8i9TVwUgvq_oH6JpiBx8I6bFM4qPZIoDOps0I; HttpOnly; SameSite=None; Secure; Path=/; Domain=api.anthropic.com,]73:23:Content-Security-Policy,42:default-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none',]23:12:X-Robots-Tag,4:none,]33:6:CF-RAY,20:9e800096785617f5-DUB,]]12:http_version;8:HTTP/1.1,}7:request;5391:4:path;22:/v1/messages?beta=true,9:authority;0:,6:scheme;5:https,6:method;4:POST,4:port;3:443#4:host;17:api.anthropic.com;13:timestamp_end;18:1775470221.7317133^15:timestamp_start;18:1775470221.7310526^8:trailers;0:~7:content;4136:{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fix a bug in the serde_json crate (serde-rs/json, issue #979 https://github.com/serde-rs/json/issues/979).\n\n## Bug Description\n\n`EnumAccess::variant` silently accepts non-string JSON object member names, \nwhich violates the JSON spec. For example, the malformed JSON `{[true]: null}` \nis parsed without error when using a custom `Visitor` that calls \n`data.variant()` via `deserialize_enum`.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nIn `src/de.rs`, the `EnumAccess` implementation's `variant` method deserializes \nthe object key using a generic `seed.deserialize(&mut *self.de)` call. This \nallows the deserializer to accept any JSON value (arrays, numbers, booleans, \netc.) as an object member name, instead of enforcing that it must be a JSON \nstring.\n\nThe relevant line is approximately:\n    let val = tri!(seed.deserialize(&mut *self.de));\n\n## Required Fix\n\nEnforce that the JSON object member key is a string before passing it to the \nseed deserializer. You should either:\n  - Parse the key as a string first and return an error if it is not, OR\n  - Use a wrapper deserializer that only accepts strings (similar to how the\n    `MapKey` deserializer is implemented elsewhere in the file)\n\nDo NOT accept non-string values as enum variant keys under any circumstance.\n\n## Regression Test\n\nAdd a test (e.g. in `tests/regression/issue979.rs`) that verifies the \nfollowing malformed JSON returns an error when deserialized via `deserialize_enum`:\n\n    {[true]: null}\n\nThe reproducer from the issue demonstrates the bug:\n\n    use serde::de::{Deserializer, VariantAccess, Visitor};\n\n    struct V;\n    impl<'de> Visitor<'de> for V {\n        type Value = (Vec<bool>, ());\n\n        fn expecting(&self, f: &mut std::fmt::Formatter) -> std::fmt::Result {\n            write!(f, \"enum\")\n        }\n\n        fn visit_enum<A>(self, data: A) -> Result<Self::Value, A::Error>\n        where\n            A: serde::de::EnumAccess<'de>,\n        {\n            let (key, variant_access) = data.variant()?;\n            let value = variant_access.newtype_variant()?;\n            Ok((key, value))\n        }\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn test_issue979_non_string_enum_key_rejected() {\n        let mut de = serde_json::Deserializer::from_str(\"{[true]: null}\");\n        let result = de.deserialize_enum(\"name\", &[], V);\n        assert!(result.is_err(), \"expected error for non-string object key\");\n    }\n\n## Files to Look At\n\n- `src/de.rs` ‚Äî specifically the `EnumAccess` impl (look for `impl EnumAccess` \n  or `visit_enum`, and the key-reading code in `variant()`)\n- `tests/regression/` ‚Äî add the new regression test here"}]}],"system":[{"type":"text","text":"x-anthropic-billing-header: cc_version=2.1.92.067; cc_entrypoint=cli; cch=498ab;"},{"type":"text","text":"You are Claude Code, Anthropic's official CLI for Claude."},{"type":"text","text":"Generate a concise, sentence-case title (3-7 words) that captures the main topic or goal of this coding session. The title should be clear enough that the user recognizes the session in a list. Use sentence case: capitalize only the first word and proper nouns.\n\nReturn JSON with a single \"title\" field.\n\nGood examples:\n{\"title\": \"Fix login button on mobile\"}\n{\"title\": \"Add OAuth authentication\"}\n{\"title\": \"Debug failing CI tests\"}\n{\"title\": \"Refactor API client error handling\"}\n\nBad (too vague): {\"title\": \"Code changes\"}\nBad (too long): {\"title\": \"Investigate and fix the issue where the login button does not respond on mobile devices\"}\nBad (wrong case): {\"title\": \"Fix Login Button On Mobile\"}"}],"tools":[],"metadata":{"user_id":"{\"device_id\":\"65343aad5d16bab6cb161b512a230bbaec090853c2ca03abbb4f2f8e6751438a\",\"account_uuid\":\"\",\"session_id\":\"28450766-579f-4289-99ba-6584ba38a808\"}"},"max_tokens":32000,"temperature":1,"output_config":{"format":{"type":"json_schema","schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"title":{"type":"string"}},"required":["title"],"additionalProperties":false}}},"stream":true},7:headers;981:29:6:Accept,16:application/json,]31:13:Authorization,10:[REDACTED],]36:12:Content-Type,16:application/json,]51:10:User-Agent,33:claude-cli/2.1.92 (external, cli),]68:24:X-Claude-Code-Session-Id,36:28450766-579f-4289-99ba-6584ba38a808,]28:16:X-Stainless-Arch,5:arm64,]25:16:X-Stainless-Lang,2:js,]26:14:X-Stainless-OS,5:Linux,]40:27:X-Stainless-Package-Version,6:0.80.0,]31:23:X-Stainless-Retry-Count,1:0,]30:19:X-Stainless-Runtime,4:node,]41:27:X-Stainless-Runtime-Version,7:v24.3.0,]29:19:X-Stainless-Timeout,3:600,]173:14:anthropic-beta,150:interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14,redact-thinking-2026-02-12,context-management-2025-06-27,prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05,structured-outputs-2025-12-15,]52:41:anthropic-dangerous-direct-browser-access,4:true,]35:17:anthropic-version,10:2023-06-01,]26:9:x-api-key,10:[REDACTED],]14:5:x-app,3:cli,]28:10:Connection,10:keep-alive,]28:4:Host,17:api.anthropic.com,]46:15:Accept-Encoding,23:gzip, deflate, br, zstd,]25:14:Content-Length,4:4136,]]12:http_version;8:HTTP/1.1,}6:backup;0:~17:timestamp_created;18:1775470221.7311978^7:comment;0:;8:metadata;0:}6:marked;0:;9:is_replay;0:~11:intercepted;5:false!11:server_conn;4101:3:via;0:~19:timestamp_tcp_setup;18:1775470221.7612765^7:address;27:17:api.anthropic.com;3:443#]19:timestamp_tls_setup;18:1775470221.7891612^13:timestamp_end;0:~15:timestamp_start;18:1775470221.7322285^3:sni;17:api.anthropic.com;11:tls_version;7:TLSv1.3;11:cipher_list;0:]6:cipher;22:TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384;11:alpn_offers;0:]4:alpn;0:,16:certificate_list;3569:1318:-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----
